{"resourceIdentifier":"2361","resourceName":"Afforestation in cooperation with local landowners for Forestal San Pedro S.A","description":"The proposed VCS grouped project “Afforestation in cooperation with local landowners for Forestal San Pedro S.A” represents one of the first major afforestation projects of the private sector in Paraguay. \r\nForestal San Pedro is a company established in 2019 by an International forestry Fund. The company aims to establish and manage an area of 8,000 ha of sustainable forest plantations for the sequestration of carbon and the production of quality timber in Eastern Paraguay. \r\nForestal San Pedro seeks to cooperate with local medium and large landowners to conduct tree planting on their properties. As a diversification strategy, plantations are largely established in silvopastoral systems on traditional cattle farms. Landowners lease their land to the company and get a share of the expected benefits. At the same time, they continue using the land for cattle grazing in a manner compatible with forestry. \r\nThe expansion strategy provides an entry point for tree planting in the degraded and deforested landscape of Eastern Paraguay, dominated by cattle grazing and mechanized soy production. Despite the need to develop new models that can address environmental degradation and climate change, while at the same time offering a sustainable supply to the national wood and timber market, the tree component is still far from integrated into the regional productive landscape. \r\nTarget production areas encompass areas deforested decades ago that have been used for implanted pastures and mechanized soy, but are now degraded. The project is interesting for cattle ranchers that need to integrate sustainable intensification into their extensive grazing models to remain competitive in the area. It is also a good opportunity for landowners having experienced a decrease in agricultural productivity due to the marginal suitability of their land for mechanized agriculture.","location":{"latitude":-23.740342,"longitude":-56.402280},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-02-13","endExclusive":"2021-03-16","endInclusive":"2021-03-15"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2361"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"San Pedro, Canindeyu"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Forestal San Pedro S.A."},{"type":"string","value":"Germany"},{"type":"string","value":"+49 761 208534 40"},{"type":"string","value":"andrea.braun@unique-forestinvestment.de"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2361"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2361"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"45549"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":104831}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-ACM0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4401 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"TÜV NORD CERT GmbH"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"29/03/2022"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 05/04/2015 - 04/04/2035"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=50977&IDKEY=llksjoiuwqowrnoiuomnckjashoufifmln902309ksdflku098o70297283","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName"